## Directory contract

```
src/
├── app/                              # routing + composition only
├── components/                       # legacy UI primitives (will migrate to shared/presentation/)
├── modules/<feature>/                # business capabilities
│   ├── domain/                       # entities, value objects, domain errors — plain TS
│   ├── application/                  # use cases, ports, DTOs, policies — no framework
│   ├── infrastructure/               # Prisma repos, provider adapters — implement ports
│   ├── presentation/                 # components, actions, schemas, view models
│   ├── composition/                  # dependency factories (createXUseCase(ctx))
│   └── index.ts                      # PUBLIC API — only path other modules may import
├── shared/
│   ├── application/                  # Result, Clock, IdGenerator, primitives
│   ├── domain/                       # cross-cutting domain concepts (rare)
│   ├── infrastructure/               # Prisma client, Redis, R2, logging, startup preflight
│   ├── presentation/                 # cn(), animations, form-state, UI atoms
│   └── testing/                      # test builders
├── composition/                      # getServerContext, module wiring
├── config/                           # env.ts (validated), routes, feature flags
└── instrumentation.ts                # startup hook → preflight
```

### Dependency direction

```
app + presentation  →  application  →  domain
                                       ↑
                    infrastructure  ───┘   (implements domain/application interfaces)
```

**Domain never points outward.** If a domain file imports from `@/shared/infrastructure` or `next/*`, the design is wrong.

---

## Per-layer contracts

### `app/` (Delivery)
- Reads cookies, headers, params, form data
- Transport-level validation (Zod schema on the wire shape)
- Calls `getServerContext()` → gets an authenticated actor + deps
- Calls **one** use case
- Maps result to view model or HTTP response
- May call `revalidatePath` / `revalidateTag` / `redirect` / `notFound`
- **Never** imports Prisma, Stripe, OpenAI, R2, Redis directly

### `modules/<feature>/application/` (Application)
- Loads entities via repository interfaces
- Runs authorization policies
- Invokes domain behavior + external service ports
- Defines transaction boundaries via `unitOfWork.run(...)`
- Returns `Result<T, E>` or DTOs
- **Never** imports `next/*`, `react`, `@prisma/client`, `stripe`, `openai`

### `modules/<feature>/domain/` (Domain)
- Entities with identity + behavior
- Value objects (`EmailAddress`, `Money`, `CreditAmount`)
- Domain services when a rule spans multiple entities
- Repository contracts (interfaces only)
- Domain errors, domain events
- **Only** imports from `src/shared/domain/` and pure standard library

### `modules/<feature>/infrastructure/` (Infrastructure)
- Prisma repository implementations
- Provider adapters (Stripe, OpenAI, R2, Resend, etc.)
- Persistence mapping between DB rows and domain entities
- Normalizes provider errors into typed application errors
- Implements interfaces declared **inward** — never invents new business rules

### `modules/<feature>/composition/` (Composition)
- The **only** place that knows about both interfaces and concrete implementations
- Exports factories like `createStartSubscriptionUseCase(ctx: ServerContext)`
- Wires Prisma repo + Stripe adapter + audit log into the use case

### `modules/<feature>/index.ts` (Public API)
- Explicit named exports of:
  - Server Actions (`export { debitCreditsAction }`)
  - Composition factories (`export { createGetCreditBalanceQuery }`)
  - View-model types (`export type { CreditBalanceViewModel }`)
- **No** exports of domain entities, repositories, adapters, or internal errors

