## The 6 SOLID rules, applied

| Principle | Concrete rule |
|---|---|
| **S**RP | One primary reason to change per file. A Server Action changes when the form changes. A use case changes when the workflow changes. A repository changes when persistence changes. |
| **O**CP | Add adapters, don't modify use cases. `ImageGenerationPort` is stable; `RunwayAdapter`, `FalAdapter`, `OpenAIAdapter` compose against it. |
| **L**SP | Every implementation of a port honours the same contract — same not-found behaviour, same timeout semantics, same normalized errors. |
| **I**SP | Prefer `CreditBalanceReader` (1 method) over a fat `CreditService` (12 methods). Give consumers what they need, nothing more. |
| **D**IP | High-level workflows depend on abstractions. Prisma, Stripe, R2, OpenAI implement the abstractions — never the other way around. |
| **Pragmatism** | Do **not** introduce an interface for every local helper. Introduce interfaces only at boundaries that are volatile, externally controlled, expensive to test, or need multiple implementations. |

